# DEPRECATED - superseded by per-service templates under
# deploy/env-templates/*.env.example. Each of the 7 BeeBase services now
# has its own production `.env`, validated independently by deploy.sh
# (see deploy/lib/env_config.sh) and loaded independently by
# docker-compose.prod.yml (see its env_file: entries and header
# comment):
#
#   deploy/env-templates/gateway.env.example    -> /opt/beebase/config/gateway.env
#   deploy/env-templates/auth.env.example       -> /opt/beebase/config/auth.env
#   deploy/env-templates/apiary.env.example     -> /opt/beebase/config/apiary.env
#   deploy/env-templates/hive.env.example       -> /opt/beebase/config/hive.env
#   deploy/env-templates/inspection.env.example -> /opt/beebase/config/inspection.env
#   deploy/env-templates/media.env.example      -> /opt/beebase/config/media.env
#   deploy/env-templates/statistics.env.example -> /opt/beebase/config/statistics.env
#
# The single shared /opt/beebase/config/.env this file used to template
# is no longer read by deploy.sh at all. Nothing deletes it
# automatically on a host that still has one from before this
# migration - it is left in place, inert, as a fallback until the new
# per-service flow is proven; see the deployment report's "remaining
# migration step" for removing it once that's confirmed.
